 "_doc": "What does the 13F `Date` column hold? Read-only check against SEC for a stratified sample of rows from the per-ticker files the live signal reads (data_prefetch/quiver/institutional/<T>.parquet): every 30th file, 7 rows per filing-delay band (Date - ReportPeriod: <=45, 46-90, 91-365, >365 days), distinct funds. Each fund was resolved through SEC full-text search to a CIK whose display name matches it, then that filer's submissions JSON gave its 13F-HR and 13F-HR/A filings for the report period. EXACT = a filing's acceptanceDateTime equals Date to the second; DATE = only the calendar date matches a filing date; NONE = filings found for the period but neither matches; UNMAPPED = no CIK or no 13F for the period found - unknown, never counted as a mismatch.",
 "verdict": "13 of 13 mapped rows match the 13F filing (11 to the second, 2 by date), 0 contradict; 15 of 28 rows did not resolve on SEC. On every row that could be mapped, `Date` is the SEC filing timestamp of the 13F-HR that carries the holding; the unmapped rows are unknown, not contradictions.",
